    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 4","answer":1,"ofParts":5,"perPart":4}, totalMarks: 4,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A reason to grant permission — any one", marks: 4, contextNote: "One reason, 4 marks.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":4,"options":["Supports technological industry in Ireland. Ireland has become increasingly technologically advanced in recent years. Continued growth and development in these areas is essential to sustainable economic growth in Ireland. •","Supports employment in the tech industry/STEM. STEM jobs represent on third of the Irish job market. Allowing additional development within this industry will continue to provide additional jobs for people in this sector. •","Source of government revenue. Data centres are in huge demand and thus highly profitable. The Irish government stands to benefit from additional taxes on earnings from these companies and their employees. •","Investment is an injection into the circular flow of income. Additional investment into the circular flow of income should be encouraged as it may have a multiplier effect, leading to further growth in the economy. •","May encourage further FDI. Some MNCs may consider locating in Ireland if they see a growth in the availability of these data centres here."]} },
    ],
